 "text": "Hi, how have you been? Fresh fruits that last few days out of season are usually fine, avocados, bananas, apples, and cut up veggies like carrots and cut up in a window box. Then keep the backpack on your back and only fill it up at stops. A full pack hangs down a lot and gets heavy quickly. A small box of crackers and cheese is easy on the immune system. Popped corn and dry fruit are also good. Often not necessary, eat right out on the trail. A good cup of coffee or tea also counts.",
